  "raw": {
    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/lp/Working%20at%20CQUni/4f4d12b50e9d145e/?locale=en_GB": {
      "title": "WORKING AT CQUNI",
      "description": "Working at CQUni Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login WORKING AT CQUNI At CQUniversity, we are a values-driven organisation committed to making a difference in local, national and international communities through our values of Engagement, Can Do, Openness, Leadership and Inclusiveness . Our success is underpinned by our diverse, experienced and highly capable workforce that can respond and adapt to an evolving, complex and fast-paced operating environment. To be a part of CQUniversity, you need to value strong mutually beneficial partnerships, operate with integrity, embrace diversity, be bold and ‘think big’, aspire to greatness and apply innovation to everything you do. If that idea appeals to you, we’d love to welcome you to the team. BE REWARDED The sky is the limit at CQUniversity. Strive for your professional goals in a supportive and encouraging environment. We invest in our most important asset – our people. Click here for further information... BE ENGAGED From community ties to global partnerships, CQUniversity staff are empowered to build mutually beneficial connections that drive real change and improves the lives of others. Click here for further information... BE WORLD-CLASS CQUniversity is recognised within Australia and the world for our research, teaching outcomes and social innovation. Click here for further information... Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
    },
    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Rockhampton-Casual-Academic-Learning-Adviser-%28ITAP%29-QLD/1357966266/": {
      "title": "Position Requirements",
      "description": "Casual Academic Learning Adviser (ITAP) Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Casual Academic Learning Adviser (ITAP) Posting Date: 23 Aug 2026 Type of Position: Casual Location: Rockhampton, QLD, AU Cairns, QLD, AU Bundaberg, QLD, AU Negotiable, AU Emerald, QLD, AU Townsville, QLD, AU Gladstone, QLD, AU Mackay, QLD, AU About this Opportunity Casual Office of the Vice-President Indigenous Engagement CQUniversity  Bundaberg, Cairns, Emerald, Gladstone, Mackay, Rockhampton, or Townsville (Negotiable – Excluding SEQ) Casual Rates Apply Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity CQUniversity is seeking dedicated Casual Learning Advisers to provide tailored tutorial assistance to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students through the Indigenous Tutorial Assistance Program (ITAP). In this rewarding role, you will deliver personalised academic support to students enrolled in SUN, STEPS, undergraduate and postgraduate programs across a range of disciplines. By mentoring students and strengthening their academic capability, you will contribute to improved learning outcomes and help foster a culturally safe, inclusive and supportive learning environment. This is a meaningful opportunity to use your expertise to empower students, build confidence and support success throughout their academic journey. Please note this is a casual pool. Your expression of interest will remain valid until 30 October 2026. You will only be contacted if appropriate casual work becomes available whilst your application is active. Position Requirements A completed qualification at the level at which you are tutoring. i.e., a minimum bachelor’s degree to tutor students studying within a Bachelor level course. Demonstrated knowledge and understanding of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander cultures and societies, and the ability to communicate sensitively and effectively Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and communities. Currently hold a Blue Card (Working with Children Positive Notice) to comply with the Working with Children (Risk Management and Screening) Act 2000 for regulated employment in education and care services. Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Friday, 30 October 2026 Job Requisition ID: 7061 Contact Details: Linda Born ISP@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, Certified copies of your qualifications, Certified copy of your Working with Children Check (Blue Card) and the names and email contact details of 2 referees. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. #CASUAL || #LI-LM1 || #LI-Hybrid || Keywords: Academic Tutor | University Tutor | Higher Education Tutor | Student Success Adviser | Academic Skills Adviser | Learning Support Officer | Study Support Tutor | Education Support Officer | Academic Mentor | Indigenous Student Support Officer | First Nations Student Support Officer | Academic Coach | Sessional Academic | Study Skills Facilitator | Tertiary Support Officer Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
    },
    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Sydney-Senior-Lecturer-Social-Work-NSW/1366184066/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer - Social Work Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Senior Lecturer - Social Work Posting Date: 21 Aug 2026 Type of Position: Continuing Location: Sydney, NSW, AU About this Opportunity Continuing, Full-Time School of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Sciences CQUniversity Sydney (Relocation support available) Total Remuneration $166,553 to $189,070 pa (including salary of $140,740 to $159,767 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity The School of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Sciences is seeking an experienced and passionate Senior Lecturer in Social Work to help shape the future of social work education and practice. As a key member of our academic team, you will be responsible for teaching and supervising undergraduate and postgraduate students, delivering high-impact education and personalised support to a diverse student cohort. You will provide leadership in the delivery and ongoing development of the Master of Social Work (Qualifying) course, inspiring and mentoring the next generation of social workers while contributing to high-impact research and scholarship. Working collaboratively with colleagues, industry and community partners, you will help ensure graduates are equipped to respond to contemporary social and community challenges and create positive change in the lives of individuals, families and communities. Join CQUniversity and make a lasting contribution to a profession that changes lives while being part of a collaborative, innovative and supportive academic community. Be Rewarded 17% superannuation (with the choice to join an award-winning superfund) 5.4 weeks annual leave (plus 3 working days paid at Christmas and New Year closure) 10 days personal/sick leave, plus 5 days carer’s leave 7.25 hours engaged service leave Fantastic professional and career development opportunities Up to 26 weeks (six months) paid parental leave Access to an Employee Assistance Program and Fitness Passport Position Requirements A doctoral qualification (PhD) in a discipline relevant to Social Work. A Bachelor of Social Work or Master of Social Work (Qualifying), with eligibility for membership of the Australian Association of Social Workers (AASW). Demonstrated ability to teach and supervise undergraduate and postgraduate students, with experience in multi-modal delivery strategies for student support. Demonstrated experience in a management level position relating to Social Work. Teaching qualification or willingness to pursue a Graduate Certificate in Tertiary Teaching/Education. Awareness of current professional and educational issues in the field. Proven research track record through recent published research outputs with the ability to contribute to research in the school. Pre-Employment Checks Appointment to this role is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, which may include a National Police Check and/or Working with Children Check (where applicable). The University is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and respectful environment where its members can study, work and live free from gender-based violence. In line with our organisational values and regulatory obligations, applicants may be required to declare any past or current allegations, investigations or findings relating to gender-based violence. The successful candidate may also be required to demonstrate that they meet the “fit and proper person” criteria as required under applicable legislation and regulatory frameworks (including ASQA requirements where relevant). Our Commitment to Inclusion At CQUniversity, inclusivity is at the heart of who we are. We are committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels respected, supported and empowered to succeed regardless of background or ability. We advance reconciliation through our Stretch Reconciliation Action Plan (RAP), First Nations Workforce Strategy and our First Nations Cultural Competency Framework , strengthening opportunities for First Nations peoples and embedding cultural respect across our organisation. Through our Disability-Informed Action Plan, we continue to enhance accessibility and inclusion across our University. As a recognised member of the Hidden Disabilities Sunflower Program , we actively promote awareness and understanding of non-visible disabilities, helping to ensure everyone can bring their whole selves to work and thrive. CQUniversity is also committed to providing an accessible, equitable and inclusive recruitment and selection process. The University will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment, selection, appointment and onboarding process to ensure people with disability can participate on an equal basis with others. Position Description For further information about this position, please refer to the Position Description . Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Sunday, 20 September 2026 Job Requisition ID: 7596 Contact Details: Sarah Wayland 0415 558 735 s.wayland@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, and a 1-2 page Cover Letter highlighting your relevant skills, experience and suitability for the position. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and CQUniversity’s domestic and international student graduates with post-study work rights are encouraged to apply. #ACADC || #LI-JF1 || #LI-Onsite || Keywords: Clinical Educator | AHPRA | Clinical Facilitator | Clinical Nurse Consultant (CNC) | Nurse Unit Manager (NUM) | Preceptor | Clinical Nurse Specialist (CNS) | Curriculum | Hospital | Simulation | Facilitation | Course Coordination | Mental Health | Community Services | Practitioner | Allied Health | Field Education | Social Worker | Melbourne | Canberra | Brisbane Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
    },
    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Cairns-Associate-Professor-Clinical-Exercise-Physiology-QLD/1366179066/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "Associate Professor - Clinical Exercise Physiology Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Associate Professor - Clinical Exercise Physiology Posting Date: 21 Aug 2026 Type of Position: Continuing Location: Cairns, QLD, AU Rockhampton, QLD, AU About this Opportunity Continuing, Part-Time (0.5FTE - 36.25hrs/fortnight) School of Health, Medical and Applied Sciences CQUniversity Cairns or Rockhampton Total Remuneration $98,294 to $107,304 pa (including salary of $83,060 to $90,674 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity CQUniversity’s School of Health, Medical and Applied Sciences delivers education and research across a range of health and applied science disciplines, with a focus on preparing graduates to meet professional and industry needs. An opportunity is available for an Associate Professor in Clinical Exercise Physiology to provide academic leadership and contribute to the development of the discipline and the Master of Clinical Exercise Physiology at CQUniversity. The role will provide leadership across teaching, research and curriculum development, including the delivery and ongoing development of undergraduate and postgraduate programs. You will contribute to course coordination, curriculum development and evaluation, undergraduate and postgraduate supervision, and the delivery of teaching across relevant units. The role will also involve developing and maintaining industry and professional networks, contributing to research and external funding, and providing academic leadership across the School and University. Be Rewarded 17% superannuation (with the choice to join an award-winning superfund) 5.4 weeks annual leave (plus 3 working days paid at Christmas and New Year closure)* 10 days personal/sick leave, plus 5 days carer’s leave* 7.25 hours engaged service leave Fantastic professional and career development opportunities Up to 26 weeks (six months) paid parental leave* Access to an Employee Assistance Program and Fitness Passport Position Requirements PhD or equivalent in Exercise Physiology, Clinical Exercise Physiology or a related discipline, with significant relevant experience. Hold, or be eligible for, AEP accreditation with Exercise and Sports Science Australia (ESSA). Demonstrated record of quality teaching, supervision and curriculum development across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Proven research capability, including high-quality publications, external funding and/or research partnerships. Demonstrated academic leadership across teaching, research, curriculum development and/or academic governance. Strong capacity to engage with industry, professional and community stakeholders and contribute positively to team culture. There will be a requirement to travel between campuses for residential school delivery during term. Pre-Employment Checks Appointment to this role is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, which may include a National Police Check and/or Working with Children Check (where applicable). The University is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and respectful environment where its members can study, work and live free from gender-based violence. In line with our organisational values and regulatory obligations, applicants may be required to declare any past or current allegations, investigations or findings relating to gender-based violence. The successful candidate may also be required to demonstrate that they meet the “fit and proper person” criteria as required under applicable legislation and regulatory frameworks (including ASQA requirements where relevant). Our Commitment to Inclusion At CQUniversity, inclusivity is at the heart of who we are. We are committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels respected, supported and empowered to succeed regardless of background or ability. We advance reconciliation through our Stretch Reconciliation Action Plan (RAP), First Nations Workforce Strategy and our First Nations Cultural Competency Framework , strengthening opportunities for First Nations peoples and embedding cultural respect across our organisation. Through our Disability-Informed Action Plan, we continue to enhance accessibility and inclusion across our University. As a recognised member of the Hidden Disabilities Sunflower Program , we actively promote awareness and understanding of non-visible disabilities, helping to ensure everyone can bring their whole selves to work and thrive. CQUniversity is also committed to providing an accessible, equitable and inclusive recruitment and selection process. The University will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment, selection, appointment and onboarding process to ensure people with disability can participate on an equal basis with others. Position Description For further information about this position, please refer to the Position Description. Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Sunday, 20 September 2026 Job Requisition ID: 7589 Contact Details: Dr Joshua Guy (07) 4037 4720 j.guy@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, and a 1-2 page Cover Letter highlighting your relevant skills, experience and suitability for the position. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and CQUniversity’s domestic and international student graduates with post-study work rights are encouraged to apply. *Pro-rata for part-time employees #ACADD || #LI-LM1 || #LI-Onsite || Keywords: University Lecturer | Senior Lecturer | Clinical Exercise Physiologist | Accredited Exercise Physiologist | Academic Leader | Allied Health Academic | Health Sciences Academic | Exercise Science Academic | Tertiary Educator | Clinical Educator | Exercise Rehabilitation Specialist | Clinical Exercise Specialist | Exercise Science Researcher | Academic Program Coordinator | Course Coordinator | Higher Education Academic | Applied Physiology | Applied Exercise Physiology | Sports and Exercise Science | Exercise Rehabilitation | Exercise Prescription | Chronic Disease Management | Rehabilitation Programs | Allied Health Education | Professional Practice Development Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
    },
    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Brisbane-LecturerSenior-Lecturer-Chiropractic-QLD/1365814466/": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Chiropractic Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Chiropractic Posting Date: 13 Aug 2026 Type of Position: Continuing Location: Brisbane, QLD, AU About this Opportunity Continuing, Full-Time School of Health, Medical and Applied Sciences CQUniversity Brisbane (Relocation support available) Lecturer (Academic B) - Total Remuneration $138,968 to $161,953 pa (including salary of $117,430 to $136,853 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) Senior Lecturer (Academic C) - Total Remuneration $166,553 to $189,070 pa (including salary of $140,740 to $159,767 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) The successful candidate will be appointed at a level that reflects their qualifications and experience. Please indicate your preferred level in your application. Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity CQUniversity is seeking a passionate academic to join our School of Health, Medical and Applied Sciences and contribute to the continued growth of our chiropractic program. Working as part of the College of Health Sciences , you will work with students, communities, industry and professional bodies to deliver innovative education and applied research that makes a real-world difference. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to the development of the chiropractic program through teaching and supervision of undergraduate and postgraduate students, curriculum development, research and scholarship, and meaningful professional and industry engagement. You will bring experience in curriculum development, quality assurance and accreditation, alongside a commitment to excellence in tertiary teaching, student success and industry engagement. You will join a growing team of chiropractic academics committed to advancing the profession and shaping the future of chiropractic education at CQUniversity. Be Rewarded 17% superannuation (with the choice to join an award-winning superfund) 5.4 weeks annual leave (plus 3 working days paid at Christmas and New Year closure) 10 days personal/sick leave, plus 5 days carer’s leave 7.25 hours engaged service leave Fantastic professional and career development opportunities Up to 26 weeks (six months) paid parental leave Access to an Employee Assistance Program and Fitness Passport Position Requirements Hold full AHPRA registration as a Chiropractor, with a relevant postgraduate qualification and minimum five years’ clinical practice experience. Demonstrated tertiary teaching experience, including curriculum development and multi-modal delivery across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Demonstrated ability to supervise students and contribute to research and scholarship aligned with School priorities. Demonstrated ability to build effective industry, professional and community partnerships. Hold, or be willing to obtain, a relevant teaching qualification (e.g. Graduate Certificate in Tertiary Education). Additional requirements for Senior Lecturer Meet the requirements for Lecturer and hold a relevant doctoral qualification. Demonstrated strong research track record, including publications, postgraduate supervision and competitive research funding. Demonstrated leadership in curriculum development, teaching innovation and academic staff mentoring. Demonstrated strategic engagement with professional bodies, industry and community stakeholders. Pre-Employment Checks Appointment to this role is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, which may include a National Police Check and/or Working with Children Check (where applicable). The University is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and respectful environment where its members can study, work and live free from gender-based violence. In line with our organisational values and regulatory obligations, applicants may be required to declare any past or current allegations, investigations or findings relating to gender-based violence. The successful candidate may also be required to demonstrate that they meet the “fit and proper person” criteria as required under applicable legislation and regulatory frameworks (including ASQA requirements where relevant). Our Commitment to Inclusion At CQUniversity, inclusivity is at the heart of who we are. We are committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels respected, supported and empowered to succeed regardless of background or ability. We advance reconciliation through our Stretch Reconciliation Action Plan (RAP), First Nations Workforce Strategy and our First Nations Cultural Competency Framework , strengthening opportunities for First Nations peoples and embedding cultural respect across our organisation. Through our Disability-Informed Action Plan, we continue to enhance accessibility and inclusion across our University. As a recognised member of the Hidden Disabilities Sunflower Program , we actively promote awareness and understanding of non-visible disabilities, helping to ensure everyone can bring their whole selves to work and thrive. CQUniversity is also committed to providing an accessible, equitable and inclusive recruitment and selection process. The University will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment, selection, appointment and onboarding process to ensure people with disability can participate on an equal basis with others. Position Description For further information about these positions, please refer to the Position Description's below: Lecturer (Academic B) – Chiropractic Senior Lecturer (Academic C) – Chiropractic Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Sunday, 13 September 2026 Job Requisition ID: 7592 Contact Details: Dr Matt Fernandez (07) 3023 4279 m.fernandez@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, and a 1-2 page Cover Letter highlighting your relevant skills, experience and suitability for the position. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and CQUniversity’s domestic and international student graduates with post-study work rights are encouraged to apply. #ACADC || #LI-LM1 || #LI-Onsite || Keywords: Chiropractor | Clinical Lecturer | Clinical Educator | University Academic | Tertiary Educator | Allied Health Educator | Health Sciences Educator | Chiropractic Practitioner | Clinical Supervisor | Course Coordinator | Program Coordinator | Discipline Lead | Academic Coordinator | Evidence Based Practice | Manual Therapy | Musculoskeletal Practice | Patient Care | Professional Practice | Health Practitioner | Healthcare Education | Academic Career | University Teaching | Clinical Training | Health Education | Healthcare Research | Practitioner Educator Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
